["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/inspection", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A thorough examination or checking of documentation, records, processes, or systems to confirm compliance or adherence. An inspection needs to have a defined set of acceptance criteria (e.g. a checklist), a documentation of roles involved in the inspection (e.g. to document the inspector's independence) and a clear documentation of when and how it was performed.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Hardware/productAgent", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The Agent who is responsible for product branding such as an OEM.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ecli", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[European Case Law Identifier (ECLI)](https://data.europa.eu/data/datasets/european-case-law-identifier-ecli) is a uniform identifier for judicial decisions across Europe. It consists of five mandatory components: the \"ECLI\" prefix, a country code, a court code, the year of the decision, and a unique serial number (e.g., `ECLI:EU:C:2023:94`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/FunctionalSafety/EvidenceRelationship", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#NodeShape", "globalId", "", ""]
